# Not part of the page. README.md documents the demo for whoever edits it next;
# tools/ holds the repo-side checks (check_shaders.py, crosscheck.py) and the
# WebAssembly build script; wasm/ holds that build's C++ inputs (the glue and the
# GL shim) and its input manifest. What the page loads is needle-core.js and
# needle-core.wasm, at the top. wrangler would otherwise upload the rest and serve
# it, which is neither useful nor anybody's business.
